#===============================================================================
#  ARDHANARISHVARA OS — ENGINEERING SUPPORT DOCUMENT
#  SovereignOS Storage Engine v4 — Erasure Coding (RS-K+M)
#  File: storage_engine_v4_erasure.support
#===============================================================================
#  PURPOSE:
#    Engineering reference for the SovereignOS Storage Engine v4:
#      • Reed-Solomon erasure coding
#      • distributed shard placement
#      • fault-tolerant reads
#      • shard repair & healing
#      • distributed snapshots
#
#===============================================================================
#  MODULE SUMMARY:
#
#    - [Erasure Coding](ca://s?q=Explain_Erasure_Coding)
#    - [Reed-Solomon K+M](ca://s?q=Explain_Reed_Solomon_K_M)
#    - [Shard Placement](ca://s?q=Explain_Shard_Placement)
#    - [Fault-Tolerant Reads](ca://s?q=Explain_Fault_Tolerant_Reads)
#    - [Distributed Snapshots](ca://s?q=Explain_Distributed_Snapshots)
#
#===============================================================================
#  FUNCTION OVERVIEW:
#
#    - create_volume(name, size_mb, nodes)
#         Creates RS(K+M) erasure-coded volume.
#
#    - write(volume_id, data)
#         Encodes data into K+M shards and distributes them.
#
#    - read(volume_id, shard_ids)
#         Reads shards and reconstructs missing ones.
#
#    - snapshot(volume_id)
#         Creates distributed snapshot.
#
#    - restore(snapshot_id)
#         Restores shard map from snapshot.
#
#    - engine_snapshot()
#         Returns engine state.
#
#===============================================================================
#  SHARD MAP FORMAT:
#
#    {
#      "EVOL-XXXX": {
#          "SHR-A": "NODE-1",
#          "SHR-B": "NODE-2",
#          "SHR-C": "NODE-3",
#          ...
#      }
#    }
#
